ID string, causing `getVideoUrl()` to produce garbage output.\n\nLooking at the specific URL format in the bug report, it starts with `https://www.youtube.com/` instead of the expected `https://youtu.be/`, which means the `id` field is storing something like `https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKvfzCyVQPe2IYg4PkugvWQ` when it should only contain a video ID.\n\nThe duplicate `https://www.youtube.com/` prefix suggests the YouTubeChannel constructor might be handling the uploader URL incorrectly—it's passing `extractor.getUploaderUrl()` which could already be a full URL, and then `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getInstance().getUrl(getId())` might be prepending another `https://www.youtube.com/` to it. the URL. But that's for channel URLs, not video URLs, so I need to focus on the video URL duplication issue instead.\n\nThe malformed URL with the duplicate domain prefix suggests something is concatenating an already-absolute URL with another base URL. I should trace where URLs get constructed or combined in the codebase, particularly in areas that handle YouTube video links. The bug report mentions receiving a video to share, which hints this might be related to how URLs are processed when they come in from external sources or deep links.\n\nLet me check if there's any URL processing happening in the MainActivity or similar entry points that could be double-prefixing URLs.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
