{"type":"assistant","uuid":"2aaf60fe-8eb0-4da1-a800-4ebd51d1efc7","session_id":"13c061ab-458d-404f-9d5d-caa688794da3","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"2aaf60fe-8eb0-4da1-a800-4ebd51d1efc7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that when \"copyurl\" is clicked in the video player, it calls `youTubeVideo.copyUrl(getContext())`, which in turn calls `SkyTubeApp.copyUrl(context, \"Video URL\", getVideoUrl())`.\n\nSo the URL that gets copied is `getVideoUrl()`, which returns `String.format(\"https://youtu.be/%s\", id)`.\n\nIf the `id` field is a valid video ID like `7MoipvBda_8`, the URL would be correct: `https://youtu.be/7MoipvBda_8`.But if the `id` field is wrong (like a channel URL or channel ID), the URL would be wrong.\n\nNow let me think about where the `id` could be set incorrectly. Looking at the `YouTubeVideo` constructors:\n\n1. `YouTubeVideo(Video video)` - sets `this.id = video.getId();` from the Google YouTube API\n\n\n2. `YouTubeVideo(String id, ...)` - sets `this.id = id;` directly\n\nFor the NewPipe path via `getDetails()`, the constructor receives `extractor.getId()` as the video ID and `extractor.getUploaderUrl()` as the channel URL, which is the correct separation.\n\nThe real issue is that `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getInstance().getUrl(id)` is designed for video IDs, not channel URLs—if it receives an already-formed channel URL instead of a raw ID, it could produce unexpected results. But looking at the user's reported bug, the malformed URL `https://www.youtube.com/https://www.youtube.com/channel/` suggests the problem might be elsewhere in how the URL is being constructed or concatenated.\n\nThe user explicitly mentions \"a video which you receive to share,\" which points to this happening when another app sends a YouTube link to SkyTube. I should investigate how SkyTube handles incoming share intents and trace through `SkyTubeApp.getUrlFromIntent()` to see if there's a code path that's mishandling the URL during the sharing process.\n\nLooking at `ExternalUrlActivity`, it extracts the URL text from the intent and passes it to `parseUrl()`, which then calls `NewPipeService.get().getContentId(url)` to extract the content ID from the received link.\n\nThe method catches RuntimeExceptions and handles them appropriately—showing error notifications if needed and returning null. Then in `openUrl()`, the parsed URL content is used to either open the content directly or view it in a browser if it can't be handled internally.\n\nFor the duplicate URL bug, I need to find where URLs are being concatenated or prefixed inappropriately. The malformed URL suggests either double-prefixing or concatenating two full URLs together, so I should search for string formatting patterns that might be combining URLs incorrectly.\n\nI'm also wondering if there's a mismatch between what the `youtubeChannel` object's `id` field actually contains versus what it should contain—perhaps when it's set to a URL instead of a channel ID, downstream processing breaks down.\n\nLooking at the `NewPipeService.getDetails()` method, I see it's passing `extractor.getUploaderUrl()` directly as the `id` parameter to the `YouTubeChannel` constructor. If that method returns a full URL rather than just the channel ID, then any code trying to construct URLs from that `id` field would produce malformed results.\n\nThe fix would be to extract just the channel ID from the uploader URL instead of passing the entire URL through. Let me trace through what `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getUrl()` does with a full URL to understand the full scope of the issue. I need to look for where URL concatenation might be happening. The duplicated `https://www.youtube.com/` pattern suggests something is prepending a base URL to an already-complete URL. Let me search for string operations that combine URLs—maybe through `+` concatenation, `String.format`, or `Uri` handling that could be causing this overlap.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
