{"type":"user","uuid":"fac7f5a2-32ad-411e-a7b4-6fcf2648ca76","session_id":"13c061ab-458d-404f-9d5d-caa688794da3","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_a5fa8d12932a4fc0961fe73d","is_error":false,"content":"/*\n * SkyTube\n * Copyright (C) 2023  Zsombor Gegesy\n *\n * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify\n * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by\n * the Free Software Foundation (version 3 of the License).\n *\n * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\n * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\n * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\n * GNU General Public License for more details.\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License\n * along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.\n */\npackage free.rm.skytube.gui.businessobjects.views;\n\nimport android.content.Context;\nimport android.view.Menu;\nimport android.view.MenuItem;\n\nimport androidx.annotation.Nullable;\n\nimport free.rm.skytube.R;\nimport free.rm.skytube.app.SkyTubeApp;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.YouTube.POJOs.YouTubeChannel;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.YouTube.newpipe.ChannelId;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.db.DatabaseTasks;\nimport free.rm.skytube.businessobjects.db.SubscriptionsDb;\nimport io.reactivex.rxjava3.android.schedulers.AndroidSchedulers;\nimport io.reactivex.rxjava3.disposables.CompositeDisposable;\n\npublic class ChannelActionHandler {\n    private CompositeDisposable compositeDisposable;\n\n    public ChannelActionHandler(CompositeDisposable compositeDisposable) {\n        this.compositeDisposable = compositeDisposable;\n    }\n\n    public boolean handleChannelActions(Context context, YouTubeChannel channel, int itemId) {\n        switch (itemId) {\n            case R.id.subscribe_channel:\n                compositeDisposable.add(YouTubeChannel.subscribeChannel(context, channel.getChannelId()));\n                return true;\n            case R.id.unsubscribe_channel:\n                compositeDisposable.add(DatabaseTasks.subscribeToChannel(false,\n                        null, context, channel, true).subscribe());\n                return true;\n            case R.id.open_channel:\n                SkyTubeApp.launchChannel(channel.getChannelId(), context);\n                return true;\n            case R.id.block_channel:\n                compositeDisposable.add(channel.blockChannel().subscribe());\n                return true;\n            case R.id.unblock_channel:\n                compositeDisposable.add(channel.unblockChannel().subscribe());\n                return true;\n            case R.id.share:\n                SkyTubeApp.shareUrl(context, channel.getChannelUrl());\n                return true;\n            case R.id.copyurl:\n                SkyTubeApp.copyUrl(context, \"Channel URL\", channel.getChannelUrl());\n                return true;\n\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    public void updateSubscribeMenuItem(@Nullable ChannelId channelId, Menu menu) {\n        setVisible(menu, R.id.open_channel, channelId != null);\n        if (channelId != null) {\n            compositeDisposable.add(SubscriptionsDb.getSubscriptionsDb().getUserSubscribedToChannel(channelId)\n                    .observeOn(AndroidSchedulers.mainThread())\n                    .subscribe((subscribed) -> {\n                        setVisible(menu, R.id.subscribe_channel, !subscribed);\n                        setVisible(menu, R.id.unsubscribe_channel, subscribed);\n                    }));\n        }\n    }\n\n    public void updateBlockingMenuItem(Menu menu) {\n        boolean visibility = SkyTubeApp.getSettings().isEnableVideoBlocker();\n        setVisible(menu, R.id.block_channel, visibility);\n        setVisible(menu, R.id.unblock_channel, visibility);\n    }\n\n    private void setVisible(Menu menu, int id, boolean visible) {\n        MenuItem item = menu.findItem(id);\n        if (item != null) {\n            item.setVisible(visible);\n        }\n    }\n\n}\n"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"9c2aa9f0-5334-40e9-ae6c-e0aa7e3d5f40","session_id":"13c061ab-458d-404f-9d5d-caa688794da3","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"9c2aa9f0-5334-40e9-ae6c-e0aa7e3d5f40","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the `ChannelActionHandler`. When the user clicks \"Copy Url\" on a channel, it calls:\n```java\nSkyTubeApp.copyUrl(context, \"Channel URL\", channel.getChannelUrl());\n```\n\nAnd `getChannelUrl()` returns:\n```java\npublic String getChannelUrl() {\n    try {\n        return YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getInstance().getUrl(getId());\n    } catch (ParsingException p) {\n        Logger.e(this, \"getChannel URL for \" + getId() + \", error:\" + p.getMessage(), p);\n        return id;    }\n}\n```If the channel's `id` field contains a full URL like `https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKvfzCyVQPe2IYg4PkugvWQ`, then:1. `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getInstance().getUrl(getId())` receives a full URL instead of a channel ID2. This factory might try to construct a URL from this \"ID\", resulting in the malformed `https://www.youtube.com/https://www.youtube.com/channel/...`\n\n\nSo the root cause is that `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory` receives an already-absolute URL instead of just a channel ID, which causes it to concatenate another base URL in front of it, creating the malformed result. The fix needs to ensure the channel's `id` field only contains the raw channel ID.\n\nLooking at where this gets set in `NewPipeService.getDetails()`, the issue is that `extractor.getUploaderUrl()` is being used directly when it should be extracting just the ID portion instead.\n\n```\n\njava\nYouTubeChannel channel = new YouTubeChannel(extractor.getUploaderUrl(), extractor.getUploaderName());\n```\n\nThe same problem appears in `VideoPager.convert()` where `item.getUploaderUrl()` gets passed to the `YouTubeChannel` constructor. I need to extract the channel ID from the uploader URL in both places rather than passing the full URL through.\n\nLooking at the bug report more carefully, the issue shows a malformed URL where a channel URL is being doubled. The root cause is that the channel ID field is receiving a full URL instead of just the ID component. I should use the `ChannelId` class to properly extract and normalize the ID from the uploader URL before storing it.\n\nExamining the `ChannelId` constructor, it only handles the `channel/` prefix but doesn't extract the ID from a complete URL like `https://www.youtube.com/channel/...`. The `getRawId()` method just returns the already-processed ID, so I need to implement the URL parsing logic to extract just the ID portion first.\n\nI'm realizing that `getChannelId().getRawId()` in `YouTubeVideo` is for accessing the channel's ID, not the video's ID—the video ID is stored directly in the `id` field. Looking back at the bug report, the malformed URL with the channel ID suggests the issue might be in how URLs are being constructed or returned.\n\nIf `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getInstance().getUrl(id)` receives a full URL like `https://www.youtube.com/channel/...` instead of just an ID, it could either pass it through unchanged, attempt to parse it and return a malformed result, or throw an exception and return the raw input. The factory is likely designed only for IDs, so feeding it a full URL would produce that duplicated URL pattern I'm seeing in the bug report.\n\nThe real problem is that channel URLs are being used as video IDs, which suggests the channel ID extraction isn't working properly when the video is created. I need to look at how the channel ID is being extracted from the uploader URL and ensure it's done correctly before the YouTubeVideo object is instantiated. I need to trace through where the `youtubeChannel` object comes from and whether its URL is being used anywhere in the video creation flow. The `ChannelActionHandler` handles channel-level actions like subscribing and blocking, so I should check if there's a code path where a channel URL somehow gets mixed into the video's `id` field during processing.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
