ed version. I should verify `getRawId()` actually returns the normalized ID string.\n\nChecking the test case shows this approach works—`ChannelId` properly strips the `https://www.youtube.com/channel/` prefix to extract just the raw channel ID like `UCF6BQExwkd4Fmk1Nx_G6Fmw`. So the fix is to create a `ChannelId` from the uploader URL and use `getRawId()` when passing it to `YouTubeChannel`. I'm realizing the `ChannelId` constructor handles the URL prefix correctly, but the issue is that `getChannelUrl()` is calling `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getInstance().getUrl()` with a full URL instead of just the ID. The simplest approach is to store the extracted raw ID directly when creating the `YouTubeChannel`, rather than passing the full URL through.\n\nFor `NewPipeService.getDetails()`, I need to create the `YouTubeChannel` with the raw ID from the channel link handler instead of the full uploader URL. I should verify that the `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory` is accessible in that file.\n\nFor `VideoPager.convert()`, I can apply the same pattern using the existing `channelLinkHandler` that's already available in the class.\n\nI need to verify how the `channelLinkHandler` is initialized in the parent `Pager` class.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
