{"type":"assistant","uuid":"3db190c3-c53d-4492-be23-a0032adc496b","session_id":"13c061ab-458d-404f-9d5d-caa688794da3","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"3db190c3-c53d-4492-be23-a0032adc496b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Patch saved to `fix-copyurl.patch`. The fix is complete:\n\n### Bug Root Cause\n`YouTubeChannel` objects were being created with full URLs (e.g., `https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxxx`) as their `id` field instead of raw channel IDs. When `getChannelUrl()` called `YoutubeChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getUrl(getId())` with this full URL, the factory couldn't parse it properly and returned the full URL unchanged, which then got concatenated with the base URL prefix producing the doubled URL.\n\n### Fix Applied (3 files)\n\n1. **`NewPipeService.java`** - Added `getChannelIdFromUrl()` that uses NewPipe's `ChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getId()` to extract the raw channel ID from any URL format. Called in `getDetails()` instead of passing `extractor.getUploaderUrl()` directly.\n\n2. **`VideoPager.java`** - Added `getChannelId()` using the existing `channelLinkHandler` to extract the raw ID from `item.getUploaderUrl()`.\n\n3. **`VideoPagerWithChannel.java`** - Same fix as `VideoPager.java`.\n\nAll changes use NewPipe's own `ChannelLinkHandlerFactory.getId()` method which correctly handles all URL formats (`https://www.youtube.com/channel/XXX`, `channel/XXX`, raw IDs). The build passes successfully."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":99233,"output_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"total_tokens":99541}}}
